From f9c742ef251744ee7a08e22c3787593a56fec3dc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Macktherealonereally <macdev@mackthessd.org>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 18:42:54 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] PersistentDataBlockService: Keep FRP off after the old screen
 lock is verified

Verifying the FRP credential only cleared FRP in memory. Setup wizards
without FRP support (Lineage's) never store a new FRP secret, so after a
reset from a build whose setup wizard set one (e.g. GMS), FRP came back
on every boot and blocked setting a screen lock. Reset the partition
secret to the default after a successful verify; boot then deactivates
FRP on its own. Setup wizards with FRP support still set their own
secret afterwards.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: If5ba5599cac238ac23880091b566a67504695742
---
 .../android/server/pdb/PersistentDataBlockService.java   | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/services/core/java/com/android/server/pdb/PersistentDataBlockService.java b/services/core/java/com/android/server/pdb/PersistentDataBlockService.java
index 5ddc442f6..f49f484f9 100644
--- a/services/core/java/com/android/server/pdb/PersistentDataBlockService.java
+++ b/services/core/java/com/android/server/pdb/PersistentDataBlockService.java
@@ -1298,6 +1298,15 @@ public class PersistentDataBlockService extends SystemService {
             synchronized (mLock) {
                 mFrpActive = false;
                 setOldSettingForBackworkCompatibility(/* isActive */ mFrpActive);
+                // The previous screen lock was just verified. A setup wizard without FRP support
+                // (like Lineage's) never stores a new secret, so FRP would come back on every
+                // boot. Go back to the default secret, which boot deactivates on its own.
+                // Setup wizards that do support FRP still set their own secret afterwards.
+                final byte[] defaultSecret = new byte[FRP_SECRET_SIZE];
+                if (!Arrays.equals(getFrpSecret(), defaultSecret)
+                        && !updateFrpSecret(defaultSecret)) {
+                    Slog.e(TAG, "Failed to reset the FRP secret to the default");
+                }
             }
             return true;
         }
